# JavaScript Rules

## File Header
```javascript
/**
 * @fileoverview ${fileDescription}
 * 
 * This file is part of the MONO design system tooling.
 * 
 * @author ${author}
 * @since ${date}
 * @module ${moduleName}
 */

'use strict';
```

## Function Documentation
```javascript
/**
 * ${functionDescription}
 * 
 * @param {${paramType}} ${paramName} - ${paramDescription}
 * @returns {${returnType}} ${returnDescription}
 * @throws {${errorType}} ${errorDescription}
 */
function ${functionName}(${paramName}) {
  ${body}
}
```

## Class Documentation
```javascript
/**
 * ${classDescription}
 * 
 * @class
 * @implements {${implements}}
 */
class ${className} {
  ${body}
}
```

## Style Rules
- Indent: 2 spaces
- Quotes: single
- Semicolons: required
- Max line length: 100 characters
- Trailing comma: ES5
- Arrow function parentheses: always
- Bracket spacing: true
- Print width: 80 characters
- Use tabs: false

## Import Order
1. Core modules (`^@core/(.*)$`)
2. Server modules (`^@server/(.*)$`)
3. UI modules (`^@ui/(.*)$`)
4. Relative imports (`^[./]`)

## Best Practices
- Use JSDoc for all function and class documentation
- Document all parameters and return values
- Include error documentation when applicable
- Use ES6+ features appropriately
- Prefer const over let
- Use meaningful variable names
- Follow camelCase naming convention
